# Director of Advancement Services — Work Sample

An interactive, independently designed work sample built for the **Director of
Advancement Services** posting at **Boston College High School** (Office of
Institutional Advancement).

**Author:** Narissara Khomkhai
**Live page:** https://narissa-pgm.github.io/BCH/

---

## What this is

A working example of how I would approach the Director of Advancement Services
role: the 27 duties in the posting, worked through against the Office of
Institutional Advancement's mission, with every figure traceable.

The artifact is organized around a single spine:

- **Overview** — the job at a glance: mission, coverage of the posting, first-year plan
- **Operations control room** — batch board, close runway, system health and data quality
- **Project portfolio** — five post-campaign projects, prioritization, a campaign-close charter, RAID and benefits
- **Seven-stop committee route** — start with office controls, then open deeper models as decisions require
- **Duty tiles** — one worked example per duty in the posting
- **Playbook** — the reconciliation layer; every number in the page is traceable here

## Important disclaimers

- This is an **independently designed sample**. It is **not** an official system
  of the Office of Institutional Advancement and **not** an adopted plan.
- All figures are **illustrative samples**, not BC High forecasts, budgets, or
  actual institutional data.
- No confidential or personally identifiable donor information is used.

## How to read it

1. Open the live page and read the Overview first.
2. Follow the seven-stop route if you want the decision-relevant path.
3. Open any duty tile for the worked example.
4. Check the Playbook for the source and reconciliation of any figure.

## Tech

Single-file HTML/CSS/JS, no build step, no external data. All content is
self-contained in `index.html`.

